Source: local. sp_rfc1867_callback() reads $_FILES[field]["tmp_name"], ["size"] and ["name"] with
Z_STRVAL_P / Z_LVAL_P, assuming scalars. For a bracketed field name (`f[]`, `attachment[file]`,
`a[b][c]`) PHP stores each of them as an array, so the validation script gets a garbage path and
size and rejects, and every such upload fails. An empty file input (UPLOAD_ERR_NO_FILE,
tmp_name "") has no temp file either, and the script is run on "" and rejects.
Walk name, tmp_name, size and error in parallel, recursively: the keys of tmp_name drive the
traversal and each sibling is looked up by the same key with a type check, so no NULL or mistyped
zval is dereferenced. Only a leaf with a non-empty tmp_name string and an error of UPLOAD_ERR_OK
has a temp file and is validated; every other leaf is skipped. Per-file behavior (fork, execve,
waitpid, SP_* environment, logging, drop or simulation) is unchanged.
Not fixed upstream as of v0.14.0. Remove it once a release handles array-valued $_FILES entries.

--- a/src/sp_upload_validation.c
+++ b/src/sp_upload_validation.c
@@ -22,6 +22,94 @@
 
 #else
 
+static zval *sp_upload_sibling(zval *container, zend_string *key, zend_ulong h) {
+  if (container == NULL || Z_TYPE_P(container) != IS_ARRAY) {
+    return NULL;
+  }
+  return key ? zend_hash_find(Z_ARRVAL_P(container), key)
+             : zend_hash_index_find(Z_ARRVAL_P(container), h);
+}
